  "summary": "Opened quotation {{v1}} (sale.order id={{v2}}) from the Quotations list. The order lines table contains exactly TWO lines, both committed with real products and 20% tax: (1) \"[FURN_6666] Acoustic Bloc Screens\", Quantity 3.00, Unit Price 295.00, subtotal £885.00; (2) \"[E-COM11] Cabinet with Doors\", Quantity 2.00, Unit Price 140.00, subtotal £280.00. There is NO stray or empty line — no \"{{v4}}\" row and no blank-product row — so nothing needed deleting, and I made no further save. The totals section on screen reads Untaxed Amount: £1,165.00, TAX 20%: £233.00, Total: £1,398.00. This matches the persisted figure: the Quotations list view showed {{v1}} with Total £1,398.00 before I opened the form, confirming both lines and prices are saved server-side. Evidence screenshot saved to s00021_final_state.png.",
